## Executive Summary — Post-Phase 1 Update

In the latest engineering iteration, **4 critical security and data resolution gaps were resolved**:

1. ✅ **Dynamic Passport Resolution Engine & Seed Data Mapping:** Replaced static dummy product fallbacks ("AERO-X Pro Fitness Dumbbell") with [PassportLoader.tsx](file:///d:/UniQR/src/components/passport/PassportLoader.tsx). On server boot, all 20 universal seed entities from `universalSeedData.ts` are automatically converted and persisted to `db.json` assigned to test user `bhramitp@gmail.com`. Non-product entities (Customer, Work Order, Asset, Warranty, etc.) dynamically map all attributes/commercial/contact/location fields to custom fields with entity-specific passport badges. Truly unregistered QRs display a clean "Unregistered Product" placeholder.
2. ✅ **Security — Secrets Removed:** All hardcoded fallback secrets (MSG91 key, Hostinger SMTP password, Razorpay keys) were purged from [server.ts](file:///d:/UniQR/backend/src/server.ts). Created `backend/.env.example` and `backend/.env`.
3. ✅ **Security — OTP Bypass Purged:** Removed the `123456` dev bypass from `/api/v1/auth/verify-otp`. Only authentic, properly generated and stored OTP codes are accepted.
4. ✅ **Type Safety & Git Hygiene:** Fixed all 9 workspace TypeScript errors (`npx tsc --noEmit` passes with **0 errors** in both `backend` and root). Created root [.gitignore](file:///d:/UniQR/.gitignore).

**Overall Platform Maturity upgraded from Level 2.0 → Level 2.4 (Managed - Hardened).**

